P-G5, spec 001 group 7 (W1): the compose policy's ec2 class, for the Author's hand.

Built from plain copies: tools/gates/compose_policy.py and tools/gates/test/test_compose_policy.py as P-G3 and P-G4
leave them (a git archive export of 23622319 with both applied, in order); edited, then diff -u with a/ and b/ labels;
never git apply. Apply it on W1's -p branch after P-G3 and P-G4, with `patch -p1 < <this file>` at the repository's
root, and commit the result byte for byte (tasks.md T171, T172).

What it holds (tasks.md T081, T087; plan.md §16, "Group 7, as built"):
  - the ec2 class among the cloud hosts' classes, and EC2's env file's template among the files the policy reads;
  - ec2-relay-block, EC2's two doors from the tunnel end: on the edge network, publishing exactly 10.42.0.20:8085 and
    10.42.0.20:4318, in EC2's profile alone, with edge's image copied to the account's registry by the lock's pin;
  - a shared service's EC2 override, "${H4_IMAGE_<SERVICE>:-<the lock's pin>}": its own service's variable alone, the
    pin inside it held to the lock as any image is; and no env file the policy reads may name an H4_IMAGE_ key, which
    only EC2's deployer writes, in its release's env file.

Its checks, on a fresh export with P-I3, P-G1, P-G3, P-I7, P-G4, P-G2, P-I4, and this patch, in that order: the
policy's own tests pass, and `compose policy: PASS` on the real tree with its five env files.
